"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_MEZOPOTAMYA:-6499-01-01:0":{"b": ["Ubaid culture (southern Mesopotamia): Ubaid culture: the first dated Ubaid phase in southern Mesopotamia begins", "25202952"], "d": ["The painted-pottery culture of crudely sedentary, temple-bearing villages in southern Mesopotamia spanning Ubaid 0 (Oueili) to Ubaid 5 (Terminal); it is followed by the Uruk period.", "28d97520"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_MISIR_NIL_SAHRA:-0299-01-01:0":{"b": ["Kingdom of Kush — Meroe period: begins", "ee436c47"], "d": ["The Meroe period, beginning with the shift of the center of Kush from Napata to Meroe (about 300 BCE) and extending to 350 CE.", "5c13abcf"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_MISIR_NIL_SAHRA:-1069-01-01:0":{"b": ["Kingdom of Kush — Napata period: begins", "fd21e916"], "d": ["The Napata-centered period of the Kushite dynasty; the center shifts to Meroe in ~300 BCE. The 25th Dynasty (Kush), which conquered Egypt, falls in this period — the dates of the 25th Dynasty are NOT in this source.", "b8938f36"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_MISIR_NIL_SAHRA:-1449-01-01:0":{"b": ["Kingdom (culture) of Kerma (Kush): ends", "95c2812c"], "d": ["A Nubian kingdom centered on Kerma below the Third Cataract; it passes through the Early Kerma (~2500), Middle and Classic Kerma phases and ends in ~1450 BCE. Honegger 2005: 'Kerma Classique (vers 1500 av. J.-C.)' a fortified settlement.", "5ea1ab25"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_MISIR_NIL_SAHRA:-1499-01-01:0":{"b": ["Napata (Jebel Barkal): begins", "fbf16715"], "d": ["Founded in the New Kingdom as a fortified outpost of Egypt; the principal city of the Kushite dynasty (Napata period 1070–300 BCE), it retained its importance throughout the Meroe period (300 BCE–350 CE).", "a384d267"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_MISIR_NIL_SAHRA:-1556-01-01:0":{"b": ["New Kingdom (beginning of the 18th Dynasty: Ahmose I): begins", "0472735f"], "d": ["The accession of Ahmose I (beginning of the 18th Dynasty/New Kingdom) is 1570–1544 BCE (2σ) in the model of Bronk Ramsey et al.", "13b3514b"]},
