"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0026-01-01:0":{"b": ["Rome, Alexandria: Roman Republic → ownerless interval", "7df67fb7"], "d": ["At the points Rome and Alexandria, ownership passes from the Roman Republic to the ownerless interval. Transition source information: death of Theodosius 17 January 395 (consulship of Olybrius and Probus): Socrates Scholasticus, Eccl. Hist. 5.26 (NPNF, newadvent.org/fathers/26015.htm); Marcellinus Comes s.a. 395: Arcadius and Honorius take over the empire divided only by their places of residence.", "5b0ba108"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0048-01-01:0":{"b": ["Marseille, Massalia: Massalia (Marseille) → Roman Republic", "a9950655"], "d": ["At the points Marseille and Massalia, ownership passes from Massalia (Marseille) to the Roman Republic. Transition source information: Caesar BC 2.22: after the city was defeated, 'conservans' and a garrison were left - the end of free allied status, Roman control.", "51e72f2c"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0085-01-01:0":{"b": ["Athens: Roman Republic period begins", "86f10b7f"], "d": ["Athens: Roman Republic period begins. This date is not a separate event; it marks the start of this period; details and sources are given below.", "deee676b"]},
