"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0132-01-01:0":{"b": ["Bergama, Pergamon: Kingdom of Pergamon (Attalid) → Roman Republic", "164fbaa9"], "d": ["At the points Bergama, Pergamon, ownership passes from the Kingdom of Pergamon (Attalid) to the Roman Republic. Transition source information: Strabo 13.4.2: 'The Romans proclaimed the country a province, calling it Asia'.", "1e50d81c"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0140-01-01:0":{"b": ["Babylon, Seleucia (on the Tigris), Uruk: Seleucid Empire → Parthian (Arsacid) Empire", "433bc35b"], "d": ["At the points Babylon, Seleucia (on the Tigris), Uruk, ownership passes from the Seleucid Empire to the Parthian (Arsacid) Empire. Transition source information: Mithradates I reaches Seleucia in July 141 and Uruk in October 141 | Source: Lendering, J., Livius.org: Mithradates I (Bagayasha page); footnote: van der Spek 1997/8: 171 | https://livius.org/articles/person/bagayasha | «In July 141, he captured Seleucia and in October he reached Uruk in southern Babylonia.»", "7c37e7d7"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0145-01-01:0":{"b": ["Corinth: Corinth period ends", "0d4e1ef0"], "d": ["Corinth: Corinth period ends. This date is not a separate event; it marks the end of this period; details and sources are given below.", "e713b7bd"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0147-01-01:0":{"b": ["Ecbatana, Hamadan: Seleucid Empire → Parthian (Arsacid) Empire", "3ceabd91"], "d": ["At the points Ecbatana, Hamadan, ownership passes from the Seleucid Empire to the Parthian (Arsacid) Empire. Transition source information: Mithradates I conquers Media (148; as reported by Justin 41.6.7) | Source: Lendering, J., Livius.org: Mithradates I (Bagayasha page); footnote: van der Spek 1997/8: 171 | https://livius.org/articles/person/bagayasha | «Mithradates conquered Media in 148 BCE and appointed Bacasis as governor»", "a34a4560"]},
