"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0309-01-01:0":{"b": ["Pasargadae, Susa: Empire of Alexander the Great (Argead nominal) → ownerless interval; Alexander IV was killed", "f3d47842"], "d": ["Alexander IV (323-310 BC), the last king of the Argead kingship, was killed together with his mother Roxane; the Empire of Alexander entry ends with this year (entry t extended). The later owner of Pasargadae and Susa was not sourced. Babylon, Uruk and Hamadan pass to Seleucus before this date.", "fd33327d"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0310-01-01:0":{"b": ["Babylon, Uruk: Empire of Alexander the Great (Argead nominal) → Seleucid Empire", "623cf14c"], "d": ["At the points Babylon and Uruk, ownership passes from the ownerless interval to the Seleucid Empire. Source transition information: Seleucus retakes Babylon (May 311); the Seleucid Era begins with this date | Source: Finkel, van der Spek, Pirngruber (BCHP 3, Diadochi Chronicle); Livius.org new reading and footnotes, footnote to Rev. iv.10' | https://www.livius.org/sources/content/mesopotamian-chronicles-content/bchp-3-diadochi-chronicle/ | «Seleucus had recovered Babylon in May 311»", "2e4e0d12"]},
