"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0322-06-10:0":{"b": ["Alexandria: Ptolemaic (Lagid) Kingdom period begins", "e3274526"], "d": ["Alexandria: Ptolemaic (Lagid) Kingdom period begins. This date is not a separate event; it marks the start of this period; details and sources are given below.", "a57c0b24"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0329-01-01:0":{"b": ["Ecbatana, Hamadan: Achaemenid (Persian) Empire → Empire of Alexander the Great (ANTIK-ISKENDER-1113-B)", "7b1734be"], "d": ["At the points Ecbatana and Hamadan, ownership passes from the Achaemenid (Persian) Empire to the ownerless interval. Source transition information: Nabonidus year 6 (550/549): Cyrus II defeats Astyages, takes Ecbatana, carries its treasury to Anshan | Source: Brown, S. C., \"Ecbatana\", Encyclopaedia Iranica VIII/1, 1997 (rev. 2011) | https://web.archive.org/web/2025/https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/ecbatana | «records that Cyrus II defeated Astyages, captured Ecbatana, and removed its treasury to Anshan»", "68589a0a"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-0330-10-22:0":{"b": ["Babylon, Uruk: Achaemenid (Persian) Empire → Empire of Alexander the Great", "6624ab48"], "d": ["At the points Babylon and Uruk, ownership passes from the Achaemenid (Persian) Empire to the Empire of Alexander the Great. Source transition information: Alexander takes Babylon (331); source Livius summary, Arrian 3.16 not read | Source: Lendering, J., Livius.org: Babylon | https://www.livius.org/articles/place/babylon/ | «In 331, the Macedonian conqueror Alexander the Great, who was fighting a war against the Persians, captured Babylon»", "69104647"]},
