"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-1474-01-01:0":{"b": ["Uruk: First Dynasty of the Sealand → ownerless interval", "a824108a"], "d": ["At the points Uruk, ownership passes from the First Dynasty of the Sealand to the ownerless interval. Transition source information: 16th century BCE: Babylonia is divided in two - the Kassites in the north, the Sealand in the south including Uruk, Ur and Larsa | Source: Zadok, R., \"Kassites\", Encyclopaedia Iranica XVI/2, 2013, pp. 113-118 (rev. 2015); chronology Boese 1982 / Brinkman 1986 | https://web.archive.org/web/2025/https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/kassites | «Babylonia was divided into two kingdoms, that of the Kassites in the north and the Sealand in the south, including Uruk, Ur, and Larsa»", "918eed44"]},
